Bootstrap: docker
From: ghcr.io/sokrypton/colabfold:1.5.5-cuda12.2.2

# ColabFold 1.5.5 -- AlphaFold2 with fast MMseqs2-based MSAs.
#
# A pull, not a build: upstream publishes a working CUDA image and there is
# nothing the lab needs to add to it. The recipe exists anyway so the image has
# provenance in git and can be reproduced after a purge, which a bare
# `apptainer pull` in somebody's shell history cannot.
#
# HARDWARE LIMIT: the upstream tag is cuda12.2, which predates sm_120, so this
# will not run on the RTX Pro 6000 (Blackwell) nodes ggpu1-[13-19]. Fine on
# L40S (sm_89) and H100/H200 (sm_90). Ask for --gres=gpu:nvidia_l40s:1.
#
# Build:  chpc-tool build colabfold

%labels
    Tool         colabfold
    Version      1.5.5
    Upstream     https://github.com/sokrypton/ColabFold
    UpstreamRef  ghcr.io/sokrypton/colabfold:1.5.5-cuda12.2.2
    Licence      MIT (code); AlphaFold2 weights CC-BY-4.0
    Base         ghcr.io/sokrypton/colabfold:1.5.5-cuda12.2.2
    GPUArch      sm_89 sm_90 only -- NOT sm_120 (cuda12.2)
    Maintainer   Craik Lab, UCSF

%post
    set -eux
    # Assert the entry point is where we think it is. Nothing else to do.
    command -v colabfold_batch

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

%test
    set -eu
    colabfold_batch --help > /dev/null

%runscript
    exec colabfold_batch "$@"

%help
    ColabFold 1.5.5.

      chpc-tool exec colabfold -- colabfold_batch in.fasta out/

    AlphaFold2 weights are CC-BY-4.0 and may be used commercially -- unlike
    AlphaFold3, which is why this is the AF2 route and not an AF3 one.

    --use_msa_server sends sequences to a PUBLIC remote MSA server. For
    unpublished designs, fetch MSAs locally with the mmseqs2 entry instead.

    Weights download on first use into the image's own cache path, which is
    read-only here; pass --data "$CHPC_LAB/data/colabfold" and populate it once
    on the login node.
